---
import { PREVIEW_PRIVACY_URL } from "@volli/shared";
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
---

<Legal
  title="Preview Agreement"
  description="The agreement for Volli’s free, invite-only 0.3 preview: no SLA, possible data loss, and your responsibilities when using agents."
  path="/legal/preview/"
>
  <p>
    This agreement is between you and Hussain Phalasiya, the operator of Volli in Ontario,
    Canada ("Volli", "we"). It covers the invite-only Volli 0.3 cloud preview for software
    development. By checking the agreement box and continuing with sign-in, you agree to it.
    If you do not agree, do not join the preview. If you join for an organization, you must
    have its authority.
  </p>

  <h2>A free, unfinished preview</h2>
  <p>
    We do not charge for this preview. There is no paid subscription or automatic conversion
    to one. Your model providers and other services may charge you under your own agreements.
    Preview access is by invitation, including Workspace invitations sponsored by existing
    preview users, subject to their invitation allowance. An invitation does not guarantee
    continued access. Do not share sign-in credentials or bypass invitation or security controls.
  </p>
  <p>
    The preview is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties to the extent the
    law allows. There is no service-level agreement (SLA), uptime commitment or guaranteed
    support. Features may break, and data may be lost or reset. Keep independent copies of
    work you cannot lose. Do not rely on the preview for critical or regulated work.
  </p>

  <h2>You direct the agents</h2>
  <p>
    Agents, including unattended Automations, can run commands, change or delete files,
    and send data to external services using the access you give them. A worktree is not
    a security sandbox. Agents can make mistakes or be misled by content they read.
    Choose their access carefully and review code, commands and other output before relying
    on it. You are responsible for the actions you authorize, the content you submit, and
    compliance with your model providers' terms. Do not use Volli unlawfully, harm others,
    access systems without permission, or interfere with the service's security.
  </p>

  <h2>Your content and cloud history</h2>
  <p>
    You keep your rights in the content you submit. We claim no ownership of your content or
    model output; we assign to you any rights we have in that output. Other people's rights
    and model-provider terms may still apply. You permit us to store, process, transmit and
    display your content only to provide, secure and support the preview and comply with law.
    We do not use it to train AI models. The model providers you choose handle requests
    under their own terms, including any retention or training settings.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloud Workspace data and Session history sync to our service providers, even when
    tools run on your own machine. History can contain code, command output and secrets.
    Every active Workspace member can see board data and shared Sessions. Read the
    <a href={PREVIEW_PRIVACY_URL}>Privacy page</a> before
    submitting data. Agreement to these terms is not consent to optional telemetry.
  </p>

  <h2>Stopping and changes</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using the preview at any time. We may change, suspend or end the preview
    or your access. Where practical, we will notify you at your account email before ending
    the preview and help you obtain a copy of your data. We do not guarantee a notice period
    or that data will remain available after an outage, reset, or security or legal suspension.
    Keep independent backups rather than waiting for an end-of-preview notice.
  </p>
  <p>
    For export or support help, email <a href="mailto:support@volli.app">support@volli.app</a>;
    for access, correction or deletion requests, email
    <a href="mailto:privacy@volli.app">privacy@volli.app</a>. There is no complete self-service
    cloud export in this preview. If you moved a local project, open Settings → Volli Cloud →
    Progress and local copies. Go back to local saves a readable cloud export before unlocking
    the earlier local copy; it is not a live sync or a complete cloud backup. Removing the app
    does not delete cloud data.
    The <a href={PREVIEW_PRIVACY_URL}>Privacy page</a> explains deletion limitations.
  </p>
  <p>
    We will publish material changes with a new agreement version and require explicit
    acceptance before further cloud access. These terms do not change the open-source
    licenses of released Volli code. Legal notices can be sent to
    <a href="mailto:legal@volli.app">legal@volli.app</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your legal rights</h2>
  <p>
    Ontario law and applicable Canadian federal law govern this agreement, subject to any
    mandatory protections where you live. Nothing in this agreement excludes rights,
    warranties or liability that the law does not allow us to exclude.
  </p>
</Legal>
